---
/**
 * Traceback landing page.
 *
 * Deliberately one file with inline styles: a landing page has no state, no
 * routing, and no shared components yet, so a build step that produces one
 * static HTML document is the whole requirement. Palette matches the app's
 * design tokens so the two don't look like different products.
 */

const APP_URL = 'http://localhost:5173/traceback'
const REPO_URL = 'https://github.com/whereissam/Traceback'

const kinds = [
  {
    label: 'FACT',
    tone: 'fact',
    body: 'Directly observed in telemetry.',
  },
  {
    label: 'CORRELATION',
    tone: 'correlation',
    body: 'Observations linked by time, process tree, or user.',
  },
  {
    label: 'INFERENCE',
    tone: 'inference',
    body: 'A hypothesis about intent. Requires human confirmation.',
  },
]

/**
 * Measured results, not illustrations. Each row is an actual run against the
 * real npm registry (or the controlled fixture, which is labelled as such).
 * Re-measure with: curl -X POST localhost:8787/api/inspect -d '{"package":"..."}'
 */
const results = [
  {
    pkg: 'esbuild@0.28.1',
    real: true,
    hook: 'postinstall: node install.js',
    events: '3',
    findings: '3 / 1 / 0',
    verdict: 'ALLOW',
    risk: 'low risk',
    tone: 'fact',
    note: 'A legitimate package with a genuine install hook. It spawns its own binary and touches nothing sensitive — so it passes.',
  },
  {
    pkg: 'lodash@4.18.1',
    real: true,
    hook: 'none declared',
    events: '0',
    findings: '— / — / —',
    verdict: 'NOTHING TO RUN',
    risk: 'no install code',
    tone: 'muted',
    note: 'Declares no lifecycle scripts, so nothing executes at install time. The honest answer is that there is nothing to detonate.',
  },
  {
    pkg: 'unknown-analytics-helper@1.4.2',
    real: false,
    hook: 'postinstall: node postinstall.js',
    events: '6',
    findings: '7 / 3 / 2',
    verdict: 'BLOCK',
    risk: 'high risk',
    tone: 'danger',
    note: 'Controlled fixture. Reads the seeded credential, sends it to an external host, and rewrites the deployment workflow.',
  },
]

const properties = [
  {
    title: 'The model cannot invent events',
    body: 'The LLM never sees raw telemetry. It receives findings already derived by deterministic rules and references them by id. Every id is checked against the set it was given; anything else is discarded before a row is written.',
  },
  {
    title: 'The verdict is a rule, not a guess',
    body: 'ALLOW / REVIEW / BLOCK is computed deterministically. A developer deciding whether to let third-party code run should be able to read the rule that produced the answer, and get the same answer twice.',
  },
  {
    title: 'It never confirms its own hypothesis',
    body: 'Every inference ships unconfirmed with a note describing what would settle it. Only a human marks it confirmed. When the canary proved transmission, the system withdrew its weaker guess rather than leaving it beside the proof.',
  },
  {
    title: 'It states what it could not establish',
    body: 'Every verdict carries a “not confirmed” list — including ALLOW, which says only the behaviour exercised during this run was observed. A gate that hides its uncertainty is more dangerous than one that has none.',
  },
]
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Traceback — a security gate for AI-installed npm packages</title>
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" sizes="any" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="/traceback-mark.png" />
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/apple-touch-icon.png" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#c96442" />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta
      property="og:title"
      content="Traceback — a security gate for AI-installed npm packages"
    />
    <meta property="og:image" content="/og-image.png" />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
    <meta name="twitter:image" content="/og-image.png" />
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Traceback runs a package's install hook in an isolated sandbox, records what it actually does, and returns ALLOW / REVIEW / BLOCK — every claim labelled FACT, CORRELATION, or INFERENCE."
    />
    <style>
      :root {
        --background: #faf9f5;
        --foreground: #3d3929;
        --card: #fffefb;
        --muted-foreground: #83827d;
        --primary: #c96442;
        --border: #dad9d4;
        --fact: #4f6b4a;
        --correlation: #6b5bc4;
        --inference: #a9701c;
        --danger: #b3261e;
        --radius: 0.5rem;
      }

      @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
        :root {
          --background: #262624;
          --foreground: #c3c0b6;
          --card: #2e2e2b;
          --muted-foreground: #b7b5a9;
          --primary: #d97757;
          --border: #3e3e38;
          --fact: #8fb08a;
          --correlation: #a394ec;
          --inference: #dba54a;
          --danger: #ef4444;
        }
      }

      * {
        box-sizing: border-box;
      }
      body {
        margin: 0;
        background: var(--background);
        color: var(--foreground);
        font-family:
          ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, sans-serif;
        line-height: 1.6;
        -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
      }
      .wrap {
        max-width: 62rem;
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: 0 1.25rem;
      }
      code,
      pre {
        font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
      }

      /* hero */
      header {
        padding: 5rem 0 3rem;
        text-align: center;
      }
      .logo {
        display: block;
        margin: 0 auto 1.5rem;
        width: 132px;
        height: auto;
      }
      /* The mark is drawn in dark ink; lift it on a dark background. */
      @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
        .logo {
          filter: invert(1) hue-rotate(180deg);
        }
      }
      .eyebrow {
        display: inline-block;
        font-size: 0.75rem;
        letter-spacing: 0.08em;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        color: var(--primary);
        border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--primary) 40%, transparent);
        border-radius: 999px;
        padding: 0.25rem 0.75rem;
        margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
      }
      h1 {
        font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 6vw, 3.75rem);
        line-height: 1.1;
        margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
        letter-spacing: -0.02em;
      }
      .lede {
        font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 2.2vw, 1.3rem);
        color: var(--muted-foreground);
        max-width: 42rem;
        margin: 0 auto 1rem;
      }
      .maxim {
        font-style: italic;
        color: var(--muted-foreground);
        margin-bottom: 2rem;
      }
      .actions {
        display: flex;
        gap: 0.75rem;
        justify-content: center;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
      }
      .btn {
        display: inline-block;
        padding: 0.7rem 1.4rem;
        border-radius: var(--radius);
        text-decoration: none;
        font-weight: 600;
        font-size: 0.95rem;
        border: 1px solid var(--primary);
      }
      .btn-primary {
        background: var(--primary);
        color: #fff;
      }
      .btn-ghost {
        color: var(--foreground);
        border-color: var(--border);
      }

      section {
        padding: 3.5rem 0;
        border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
      }
      h2 {
        font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 3vw, 1.9rem);
        margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
        letter-spacing: -0.01em;
      }
      .sub {
        color: var(--muted-foreground);
        margin: 0 0 2rem;
        max-width: 44rem;
      }

      pre.term {
        background: var(--card);
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        border-radius: var(--radius);
        padding: 1rem 1.15rem;
        overflow-x: auto;
        font-size: 0.82rem;
        line-height: 1.65;
        margin: 0;
      }
      .muted {
        color: var(--muted-foreground);
      }

      .grid {
        display: grid;
        gap: 1rem;
      }
      @media (min-width: 720px) {
        .grid-3 {
          grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
        }
        .grid-2 {
          grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
        }
      }
      .card {
        background: var(--card);
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        border-radius: 0.75rem;
        padding: 1.25rem;
      }
      .card h3 {
        margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
        font-size: 1rem;
      }
      .card p {
        margin: 0;
        color: var(--muted-foreground);
        font-size: 0.9rem;
      }

      table.results {
        width: 100%;
        border-collapse: collapse;
        font-size: 0.86rem;
      }
      table.results th {
        text-align: left;
        font-size: 0.68rem;
        letter-spacing: 0.08em;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        color: var(--muted-foreground);
        font-weight: 700;
        padding: 0 0.7rem 0.5rem 0;
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
      }
      table.results td {
        padding: 0.7rem 0.7rem 0.7rem 0;
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
        vertical-align: top;
      }
      table.results .pkg {
        font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
        font-size: 0.8rem;
        color: var(--foreground);
        white-space: nowrap;
      }
      table.results .hook {
        font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
        font-size: 0.76rem;
        color: var(--muted-foreground);
      }
      .tag-real,
      .tag-fixture {
        display: inline-block;
        font-size: 0.6rem;
        font-weight: 700;
        letter-spacing: 0.05em;
        padding: 0.1rem 0.36rem;
        border-radius: 0.25rem;
        margin-left: 0.4rem;
        vertical-align: middle;
      }
      .tag-real {
        color: var(--fact);
        background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--fact) 15%, transparent);
      }
      .tag-fixture {
        color: var(--muted-foreground);
        background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--muted-foreground) 15%, transparent);
      }
      .v-fact {
        color: var(--fact);
        font-weight: 700;
      }
      .v-danger {
        color: var(--danger);
        font-weight: 700;
      }
      .v-muted {
        color: var(--muted-foreground);
        font-weight: 700;
      }
      .row-note {
        font-size: 0.78rem;
        color: var(--muted-foreground);
        margin: 0.3rem 0 0;
        max-width: 34rem;
      }
      @media (max-width: 820px) {
        table.results thead {
          display: none;
        }
        table.results tr {
          display: block;
          padding: 0.8rem 0;
          border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
        }
        table.results td {
          display: block;
          border: 0;
          padding: 0.12rem 0;
        }
      }

      .badge {
        display: inline-block;
        font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
        font-size: 0.7rem;
        font-weight: 700;
        padding: 0.15rem 0.45rem;
        border-radius: 0.25rem;
        margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
      }
      .fact {
        color: var(--fact);
        background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--fact) 15%, transparent);
      }
      .correlation {
        color: var(--correlation);
        background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--correlation) 15%, transparent);
      }
      .inference {
        color: var(--inference);
        background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--inference) 15%, transparent);
      }

      .verdict {
        border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--danger) 50%, transparent);
        background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--danger) 10%, transparent);
        border-radius: 0.75rem;
        padding: 1.25rem;
      }
      .verdict .tag {
        color: var(--danger);
        font-weight: 800;
        font-size: 1.15rem;
        letter-spacing: 0.02em;
      }

      ul.plain {
        margin: 0;
        padding-left: 1.1rem;
        color: var(--muted-foreground);
        font-size: 0.9rem;
      }
      ul.plain li {
        margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
      }

      footer {
        border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
        padding: 2.5rem 0 4rem;
        color: var(--muted-foreground);
        font-size: 0.85rem;
      }
      footer a {
        color: var(--primary);
      }
    </style>
  </head>

  <body>
    <div class="wrap">
      <header>
        <img
          src="/traceback-mark.png"
          alt="Traceback"
          width="132"
          height="132"
          class="logo"
        />
        <span class="eyebrow">Runtime inspection for npm install hooks</span>
        <h1>Do not trust what the package says.<br />Observe what it does.</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Your AI coding agent asks permission to run <code>npm install</code>.
          That permission does not cover the code npm runs on the package's
          behalf.
        </p>
        <p class="maxim">
          Telemetry proves. Rules correlate. AI explains. You decide.
        </p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href={APP_URL}>Open the app</a>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={REPO_URL}>Read the code</a>
        </div>
      </header>

      <section>
        <h2>The gap</h2>
        <p class="sub">
          A package can declare a lifecycle script that npm executes
          automatically during installation — and it can arrive through a
          dependency of a dependency, where nothing at the top level looks
          unusual.
        </p>
        <pre class="term"><code>{`{ "scripts": { "postinstall": "node postinstall.js" } }`}</code></pre>
        <p class="sub" style="margin-top:1.25rem">
          That script is ordinary code on your machine. It can spawn processes,
          read <code>.env</code> or <code>~/.ssh</code>, call out to the
          network, and rewrite <code>.github/workflows</code>. None of it
          appeared in the prompt you approved.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>What you get back</h2>
        <p class="sub">
          Traceback runs the hook in an isolated sandbox and returns a decision
          with its evidence attached. Verbatim output, only line-wrapped:
        </p>
        <div class="verdict">
          <div class="tag">BLOCK — high risk</div>
          <p style="margin:.5rem 0 1rem">
            A synthetic credential was read and observed leaving the sandbox.
          </p>
          <p style="margin:0 0 .35rem">
            <span class="badge fact">FACT</span>
            <span class="muted"
              >&nbsp;Synthetic credential was transmitted externally</span
            >
          </p>
          <p style="margin:0 0 1rem">
            <span class="badge fact">FACT</span>
            <span class="muted"
              >&nbsp;Deployment configuration modified by a lifecycle script</span
            >
          </p>
          <div class="grid grid-2">
            <div>
              <strong style="font-size:.8rem;color:var(--fact)">CONFIRMED</strong>
              <ul class="plain" style="margin-top:.4rem">
                <li>
                  The seeded canary appeared in the payload sent to an external
                  host.
                </li>
                <li>Build files written: .github/workflows/deploy.yml</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div>
              <strong style="font-size:.8rem;color:var(--inference)"
                >NOT CONFIRMED</strong
              >
              <ul class="plain" style="margin-top:.4rem">
                <li>
                  Whether those changes were committed, pushed, or later
                  executed.
                </li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>


      <section>
        <h2>Run against real packages</h2>
        <p class="sub">
          The same pipeline, pointed at the actual npm registry. A detector that
          flags everything is useless, so the important row is the first one —
          a legitimate package with a genuine install hook that
          <strong>passes</strong>.
        </p>

        <table class="results">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Package</th>
              <th>Install hook</th>
              <th>Events</th>
              <th>F / C / I</th>
              <th>Verdict</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {
              results.map((r) => (
                <tr>
                  <td>
                    <span class="pkg">{r.pkg}</span>
                    <span class={r.real ? 'tag-real' : 'tag-fixture'}>
                      {r.real ? 'REAL' : 'FIXTURE'}
                    </span>
                    <p class="row-note">{r.note}</p>
                  </td>
                  <td class="hook">{r.hook}</td>
                  <td class="hook">{r.events}</td>
                  <td class="hook">{r.findings}</td>
                  <td>
                    <span
                      class={
                        r.tone === 'danger'
                          ? 'v-danger'
                          : r.tone === 'fact'
                            ? 'v-fact'
                            : 'v-muted'
                      }
                    >
                      {r.verdict}
                    </span>
                    <div class="hook">{r.risk}</div>
                  </td>
                </tr>
              ))
            }
          </tbody>
        </table>

        <p class="sub" style="margin-top:1.5rem">
          <strong>F / C / I</strong> = facts, correlations, inferences. Every
          number above came from an actual run — reproduce any row with:
        </p>
        <pre class="term"><code>{`curl -X POST localhost:8787/api/inspect -d '{"package":"esbuild"}'`}</code></pre>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Every claim is ranked by how much it asserts</h2>
        <p class="sub">
          So a reader never has to guess how much the system is claiming.
        </p>
        <div class="grid grid-3">
          {
            kinds.map((k) => (
              <div class="card">
                <span class={`badge ${k.tone}`}>{k.label}</span>
                <p>{k.body}</p>
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </div>
        <p class="sub" style="margin-top:1.5rem">
          An inference cannot exist without a correlation beneath it, and a
          correlation cannot exist without facts beneath that. Remove the
          evidence and the conclusion disappears with it — a structural rule,
          with a test.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>The canary</h2>
        <p class="sub">
          “Was the secret actually sent?” is normally unanswerable from timing
          alone. So the sandbox seeds a recognisable synthetic token into the
          credential file before the install runs. If that exact token appears
          in what leaves the container, transmission is observed — not inferred.
        </p>
        <pre class="term"><code><span class="muted">without the canary</span>
<span style="color:var(--inference)">INFERENCE</span>  Possible credential exfiltration        <span class="muted">(medium)</span>

<span class="muted">with it</span>
<span style="color:var(--fact)">FACT</span>       Synthetic credential transmitted off-host  <span class="muted">(high)</span></code></pre>
        <p class="sub" style="margin-top:1.25rem">
          And when the fact appears, the system <strong>withdraws</strong> the
          inference rather than leaving a guess sitting next to the proof.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Why this isn't a model summarising logs</h2>
        <div class="grid grid-2">
          {
            properties.map((p) => (
              <div class="card">
                <h3>{p.title}</h3>
                <p>{p.body}</p>
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Honest about its limits</h2>
        <p class="sub">
          A security tool that hides what it cannot establish has missed its own
          point.
        </p>
        <ul class="plain">
          <li>
            Telemetry is currently self-reported by the simulation, not captured
            from the kernel. Syscall capture is the next step.
          </li>
          <li>
            The canary proves transmission only because we control it. A package
            that encrypts its payload would defeat it — and exfiltration would
            correctly fall back to an inference. It under-claims rather than
            over-claims.
          </li>
          <li>
            Local <code>--ignore-scripts</code> interception isn't built yet. The
            sandbox path is real.
          </li>
          <li>One host, one session. No cross-host correlation.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <footer>
        <p>
          All suspicious behaviour is simulated inside an isolated sandbox using
          synthetic secrets. No real credentials or external systems are
          accessed.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href={REPO_URL}>Source</a> · MIT licensed · Built with Astro,
          React, Hono, Supabase, Modal and OpenAI.
        </p>
      </footer>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
